{"timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:59:51.749Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_FqE5pCQjabyAB7bdpJZSNeyV","output":"Chunk ID: ffd56e\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 2110\nOutput:\n# Design: `entire migrate --checkpoints v2`\n\n## Purpose\n\nMigrate v1 checkpoint data (stored on `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch) to v2 split refs (`refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main` and `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/current`). This is a one-time upgrade operation for repositories with existing v1 checkpoint history.\n\n## Command\n\n```\nentire migrate --checkpoints v2\n```\n\n- `--checkpoints` is a required string flag. Only `\"v2\"` is accepted for now; other values return an error.\n- Leaves the v1 branch untouched after migration. Cleanup is a separate concern.\n\n## Approach: Read v1, Write via V2GitStore\n\nThe migration reads checkpoints from the v1 `GitStore` and writes them through `V2GitStore.WriteCommitted()`. This reuses the full v2 write path (validation, dual-write, generation rotation) and guarantees format consistency with natively-created v2 data.\n\n### Preconditions\n\n1. Must be in a git repository.\n2. The v1 branch (`entire/checkpoints/v1`) must exist. If not, print \"Nothing to migrate: no v1 checkpoints found\" and exit 0.\n3. v2 refs are created lazily by the v2 store's `ensureRef()` — no pre-existence check needed.\n\n### Per-Checkpoint Flow\n\n```\nv1 GitStore.ListCommitted()\n  → for each checkpoint ID:\n      1. V2GitStore.ReadCommitted(id) — if non-nil, skip (already migrated)\n      2. GitStore.ReadCommitted(id) — get CheckpointSummary from v1\n      3. For each session index (0..N):\n         a. GitStore.ReadSessionContent(id, index) — get metadata, transcript, prompts\n         b. Attempt compact transcript via agent.CompactTranscript(transcript, agentType)\n            - On failure: log warning, set CompactTranscript = nil\n         c. Build WriteCommittedOptions from session content fields\n      4. V2GitStore.WriteCommitted(opts) — dual-write to /main + /full/current\n```\n\n### Field Mapping (v1 SessionContent → WriteCommittedOptions)\n\n| v1 CommittedMetadata field      | WriteCommittedOptions field       |\n|---------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n| CheckpointID                    | CheckpointID                      |\n| SessionID                       | SessionID                         |\n| Strategy                        | Strategy                          |\n| Branch                          | Branch                            |\n| (SessionContent.Transcript)     | Transcript                        |\n| (SessionContent.Prompts)        | Prompts (string → []string split) |\n| FilesTouched                    | FilesTouched                      |\n| CheckpointsCount                | CheckpointsCount                  |\n| Agent                           | Agent                             |\n| Model                           | Model                             |\n| TurnID                          | TurnID                            |\n| TokenUsage                      | TokenUsage                        |\n| SessionMetrics                  | SessionMetrics                    |\n| InitialAttribution              | InitialAttribution                |\n| Summary                         | Summary                           |\n| CheckpointTranscriptStart       | CheckpointTranscriptStart         |\n| TranscriptIdentifierAtStart     | TranscriptIdentifierAtStart       |\n| IsTask                          | IsTask                            |\n| ToolUseID                       | ToolUseID                         |\n| (compacted bytes or nil)        | CompactTranscript                 |\n\n### Task Metadata\n\nTask checkpoints have additional files under `tasks/<tool-use-id>/` in the v1 tree (subagent transcripts, incremental checkpoint JSONs). During migration, these files are copied to the equivalent path in the v2 `/full/current` ref via tree surgery — same relative location, just on the v2 ref instead of v1.\n\n### Multi-Session Checkpoints\n\nHandled naturally by the session index loop. The first session's `WriteCommitted` creates the checkpoint entry; subsequent sessions append under incrementing session indices (the v2 store handles index assignment).\n\n### Generation Rotation\n\nTriggers naturally at the 100-checkpoint boundary during migration. This is the intended v2 behavior and requires no special handling.\n\n### Compact Transcript Generation\n\nMigration attempts to generate `transcript.jsonl` (Entire Transcript Format) from raw transcripts for each session. This is best-effort:\n- Success: `transcript.jsonl` is written to `/main` alongside metadata.\n- Failure (unknown agent type, malformed transcript, etc.): logged as a warning, migration continues without compact transcript for that checkpoint.\n\n## Idempotency\n\nBefore writing each checkpoint, the migration checks `V2GitStore.ReadCommitted(id)`. If the checkpoint already exists in v2, it is skipped. This means:\n- Interrupted migrations can be resumed by re-running the command.\n- Running migration twice produces no duplicate data.\n- The check is per-checkpoint-ID presence on the v2 `/main` ref.\n\n## Output & Progress\n\n```\nMigrating v1 checkpoints to v2...\n  [12/47] Migrating checkpoint a3b2c4d5e6f7... done\n  [13/47] Migrating checkpoint f1e2d3c4b5a6... done (compact transcript skipped)\n  [14/47] Migrating checkpoint 1122334455aa... skipped (already in v2)\n  [15/47] Migrating checkpoint 99887766aabb... failed\n\nMigration complete: 44 migrated, 2 skipped, 1 failed\n1 checkpoint failed to migrate. Check .entire/logs/ for details.\n```\n\n### Outcome Categories\n\n| Outcome                        | Stdout message                       | Log level        | Exit code |\n|--------------------------------|--------------------------------------|------------------|-----------|\n| Migrated successfully          | `done`                               | `logging.Info`   | 0         |\n| Migrated, compaction failed    | `done (compact transcript skipped)`  | `logging.Warn`   | 0         |\n| Skipped (already in v2)        | `skipped (already in v2)`            | `logging.Debug`  | 0         |\n| Failed to read/write           | `failed`                             | `logging.Error`  | 1         |\n\n- Single checkpoint failures do not abort the migration. All remaining checkpoints are processed.\n- If any checkpoint fails, the command exits with code 1 and directs the user to check `.entire/logs/`.\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- **No v1 branch:** Clean exit 0 with message \"Nothing to migrate: no v1 checkpoints found\".\n- **Invalid flag value:** `--checkpoints v3` returns an error immediately.\n- **Not a git repo:** Standard CLI error pattern (SilentError with user-friendly message).\n- **Per-checkpoint failure:** Log error, continue, summarize failures at end, exit 1.\n- **Logging:** Uses the standard `logging` package. Debug logs go to `.entire/logs/`. No custom log destinations.\n\n## File Organization\n\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go`** — Command definition (`newMigrateCmd()`) and migration orchestration logic.\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/migrate_test.go`** — Unit tests.\n- **`cmd/entire/cli/root.go`** — Register `newMigrateCmd()` via `cmd.AddCommand()`.\n\nNo new packages needed. The migration logic is glue between existing `GitStore` (v1 read) and `V2GitStore` (v2 write) APIs.\n\n## Testing\n\nAll tests in `migrate_test.go`, using `testutil.InitRepo` for git isolation and `t.Parallel()`.\n\n| Test case                       | What it validates                                                        |\n|---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Basic migration                 | v1 checkpoints appear in v2 `/main` and `/full/current` with correct structure |\n| Idempotency                     | Second run skips all, no duplicate entries                               |\n| Multi-session checkpoint        | Both sessions appear in v2 with correct indexing                         |\n| Task metadata                   | `tasks/` subtree appears at equivalent path in v2 `/full/current`        |\n| Compaction failure              | Migration succeeds without `transcript.jsonl` on `/main`                 |\n| Partial failure resilience      | Corrupt checkpoint skipped, others migrate, exit code 1                  |\n| No v1 branch                    | Clean exit with \"nothing to migrate\" message                             |\n| Invalid flag value              | `--checkpoints v3` returns error                                         |\n\nNo E2E tests — this is a pure data transformation with no agent interaction.\n"}}
