{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T00:02:57.114Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The redundancy was mostly “doing the same expensive Git/transcript work again under a new path,” not the generation batch size.\n\n1. `/full` raw transcripts were being re-chunked and re-stored during migration even though v1 already had the same transcript blobs. Now v1 reads expose `TranscriptBlobHashes` and migration reuses them when writing v2 raw transcript entries: [committed.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go:1062), [migrate.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:1080).\n\n2. Generation metadata was rescanning raw transcripts for timestamps after migration had already loaded checkpoint metadata. That showed up as `pack_full.generation_timestamps_total` at ~33s. Now archived generation metadata uses migrated session `CreatedAt` first: [migrate.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:958).\n\n3. Compact transcript offset calculation was compacting twice for checkpoints with nonzero `CheckpointTranscriptStart`: once for the full compact transcript, then again for the scoped suffix just to compute the offset. Now migration caches raw transcript position to compact line offset for same-session checkpoints and only falls back to the second compact when needed: [migrate.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:722), [migrate.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:1440).\n\n4. `/main` batch flush was still doing repeated tree surgery and summary aggregation checkpoint-by-checkpoint. The batch size was 100, but each batch still rewrote/spliced checkpoint trees one at a time. Now it builds checkpoint subtrees and applies all changes in one root update, with a fresh-checkpoint path that aggregates summary fields from the batch instead of reading blobs it just wrote: [v2_committed.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go:70), [v2_committed.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_committed.go:173).\n\n5. Fresh migrations were still checking v2 checkpoint summaries one checkpoint at a time. Now migration builds a v2 presence index once and only reads v2 summaries for checkpoints that actually exist: [migrate.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:304), [migrate.go](/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:795).","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
